From 432a7b04c14fa08a23efbfb5a18a5cf45b14afc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 04:30:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add BindingNavigator (data-navigation toolbar)

BindingNavigator was entirely absent - a compile break on any designer-
generated data-bound form that includes a navigator. Implement it as a
ToolStrip subclass that wires the standard items (move first/previous/next/
last, add, delete, a position text box and a count label) to a BindingSource:
clicking an item drives the source, the position/count readouts track the list
via PositionChanged/CurrentChanged/ListChanged, enabled state reflects the
current position, and the position box accepts a typed row number on Enter or
focus loss. Follows the WinForms surface - WireUpButton-style item-property
setters, AddStandardItems, RefreshItemsCore, the RefreshItems event, and
ISupportInitialize BeginInit/EndInit.

Covered by BindingNavigatorFunctionalTests (standard-item set, position/count
readout, move navigation, enabled state at the ends, source-driven refresh,
delete, count format, and the RefreshItems event).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
